\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Overview of all requirements utilized to define the fiducial phase space. \relax }}{95}{table.caption.240}
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Summary of different SM signal models. The MC samples are from full Run 2 yearly productions (2016, 2017 and 2018) assuming $m_{\rm H} = 125.09\GeV $. Luminosity averaged fiducial acceptance ($\mathcal {A}_{\rm fid}$) defined the fraction of events passing fiducial phase space selections, reconstruction efficiency ($\epsilon $) represented by the ratio of reconstructed to accepted events. Also, $f_{\rm nonfid}$ which are reconstructed events but does not pass fiducial phase space definition at generator level. Values are obtained using 13\hspace {0.25em plus 0.125em minus 0.08em}\ignorespaces TeV signal models and the uncertainties shown are only statistical uncertainties. \relax }}{96}{table.caption.241}
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Cross sections for \ensuremath {\ensuremath {\mathrm {q}}\bar {\ensuremath {\mathrm {q}}}\to \mathrm {Z}\mathrm {Z}}\hspace {0.25em plus 0.125em minus 0.08em}\ignorespaces production at 13 \TeV \relax }}{99}{table.caption.251}
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.4}{\ignorespaces The contribution of reducible background processes in the signal region predicted from measurements in 2016, 2017 and 2018 data using the OS method. The predictions correspond to 35.9, 41.5 and 59.7\hspace {0.25em plus 0.125em minus 0.08em}\ignorespaces fb$^{-1}$ of data at $13$\hspace {0.25em plus 0.125em minus 0.08em}\ignorespaces TeV, respectively.\relax }}{107}{table.caption.266}
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.5}{\ignorespaces The OS/SS ratios used to estimate the number of ZX events with the SS method for each final state in all three years. \relax }}{111}{table.caption.276}
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.6}{\ignorespaces Summary of the results given by the two methods for the prediction of the contribution of reducible background processes in the signal region for all three years. The weighted mean value of the results of the two methods is taken as the final estimate of this contribution, while the uncertainty of the result covers the uncertainties of both methods. The table shows symmetric individual uncertainties for the two methods, while these are treated as asymmetric in the combination and statistical analysis. Results are given for an integrated luminosity of 35.9, 41.5 and 59.7\hspace {0.25em plus 0.125em minus 0.08em}\ignorespaces fb$^{-1}$ in 2016, 2017 and 2018 data, respectively. \relax }}{113}{table.caption.283}
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.7}{\ignorespaces Number of observed candidates, expected background and the signal events passing all selections in mass range $m_{4\ell } > 70 \GeV $ corresponding to three different years. Z+X is estimated by control regions in the data while ZZ and signal events are estimated using MC simulation. \relax }}{116}{table.caption.286}
